  [OK] 1b  S_DE(r) = (r/L) A(r)/(4G) in every D (volume law overtakes area law exactly at r = L)

2-3  potential and removed entropy
  [OK] 2   Phi = -8 pi G M/((D-2) Omega r^(D-3)) has flux 8 pi G (D-3) M/(D-2), the D-dim weak-field Gauss law (f01: lap Phi = 8 pi G (d-2) rho/(d-1), d = D-1)
  [OK] 3   dS_M/dr = Phi (dA/dr)/(4G) = -2 pi M, independent of r AND of D (the Bekenstein form S_M = -2 pi M r)
  [OK] 3b  V_M = -S_M V0 = 8 pi G M r L/(D-1)

4  displacement premise u = Phi L
  [OK] 4a  V*_M = -u A = 8 pi G M r L/(D-2)
  [OK] 4b  V*_M/V_M = (D-1)/(D-2)  (paper's eq. 4.37)

5  elastic inclusion
  [OK] 5a  eps = u' = N V0/V(r) exactly (the (D-1)/(D-2) is what makes the strain at the inclusion boundary equal 1)
  [OK] 5b0 dV/dr = A(r) (so int eps^2 A dr = int eps^2 dV)
  [OK] 5b  int eps^2 dV over the exterior of the inclusion = N V0 when V(r0) = N V0, for every D (paper's eq. 4.44)
     (mutation: without the (D-1)/(D-2) factor the strain at the boundary is not 1:  eps V/(N V0) = (D - 2)/(D - 1) )
  [OK] 5c  mutation: u = -N V0/A (no displacement factor) gives boundary strain (D-2)/(D-1), which is never 1: the factor (D-1)/(D-2) is what the premise u = Phi L supplies

